From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] makepanda: detect manylinux_2_39_riscv64

makepanda.py's own PLATFORM detection (used for --wheel's platform tag)
recognizes manylinux1/2010/2014/2_24/2_28 by checking for a specific
versioned /lib64/libc-X.Y.so file plus, for 2_28, /etc/almalinux-release.
None of those checks can ever match quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_39_riscv64
(Rocky 10): modern glibc no longer ships a libc-X.Y.so symlink at all, and
riscv64 isn't one of the arches any existing branch maps to a tag (the
2_28 branch's "else" even raises for an unrecognized arch). Detection
falls through to the generic, non-cross-compiling branch, which just
takes sysconfig.get_platform() verbatim ("linux-riscv64"), so --wheel
produces a plain linux_riscv64-tagged wheel instead of a manylinux one.

Add a branch keyed on the target arch instead of a libc filename, mirroring
the existing per-release branches' shape.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; needs a riscv64 CI leg upstream doesn't have yet to validate against]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/makepanda/makepanda.py b/makepanda/makepanda.py
index ad6230f..c80e4c6 100755
--- a/makepanda/makepanda.py
+++ b/makepanda/makepanda.py
@@ -533,6 +533,12 @@ elif target == 'linux' and os.path.isfile("/lib64/libc-2.28.so") and os.path.isf
     else:
         raise RuntimeError('Unhandled arch %s, please file a bug report!' % (target_arch))
 
+elif target == 'linux' and target_arch == 'riscv64' and os.path.isdir("/opt/python"):
+    # manylinux_2_39_riscv64 (quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_39_riscv64, Rocky 10): glibc
+    # no longer ships the versioned libc-X.Y.so file the checks above rely on, so
+    # detect this image by arch instead.
+    PLATFORM = 'manylinux_2_39-riscv64'
+
 elif not CrossCompiling():
     if HasTargetArch():
         # Replace the architecture in the platform string.
